# cipaord_endo.mmt: CiPAORdv1.0 endocardial myocyte (Myokit format) for the as-data-sets
# repository (github.com/paulcon/as-data-sets), data set CiPA_Ventricular_Proarrhythmia_Metrics.
#
# Licence: MIT for the new parts; the O'Hara-Rudy (ORd) parts are BSD 3-clause,
# copyright T. O'Hara and Y. Rudy (notice below; see also LICENSE-ORd beside this file).
# The ORd core of this file (camk, rev, ina, inal, ito, ical, iks, ik1, inaca, inak,
# background, ryr, fluxes, conc, cell, phys) follows the O'Hara-Rudy reference
# implementation as distributed in github.com/FDA/CiPA,
# AP_simulation/models/newordherg_qNet.c (commit 539ff80), whose header carries the
# notice reproduced here. The hERG/drug-binding section (ikr), the virtual-drug scaling
# (drug), the qNet integral (qnet) and the stimulus are new (MIT): the hERG Markov model is
# written in flux form from Li et al. (2017), with parameter values from the FDA files.
# No code of the FDA's own (GPL-3.0) contributions to that C file is included.
#
# Notice and disclaimer of the O'Hara-Rudy code, reproduced exactly as in the header of
# newordherg_qNet.c:
#
# Copyright (c) 2011-2015 by Thomas O'Hara, Yoram Rudy, 
#                            Washington University in St. Louis.
